MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The locking nuts fit my repeated interest in bolts, rivets and threaded inserts because they could help keep my assemblies secure; I would check that the SAE sizes match my hardware.",
    "The steel-reinforced epoxy feels useful for small metal repairs alongside my drilling and fastening supplies, giving it a clear purpose in my workshop."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The filament assumes a printing need I have not shown. Buying tools and repair supplies does not mean I have a compatible printer or a project that needs printed parts.",
    "The digital caliper fits my measuring needs, but I recently acquired one, so another would duplicate a tool I already have."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in hands-on projects seems to have been stretched into an interest in 3D printing, even though my recent purchases point toward fastening, mounting and repairs.",
    "The many filament colors and finishes all depend on the same unsupported assumption; changing the appearance does not make them useful for my current work."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of fastener assortments and installation tools suggest that compatible sizes and a clear assembly purpose matter more to me than a broad connection to making things.",
    "What I already own matters: a complementary repair supply can add a useful capability, while a second recently purchased measuring tool needs a specific reason to replace the first."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my fastening and repair work but inferred a printing hobby without evidence and missed that I already own a caliper."
}
